# 4. `pointInTriangle` — exact expression

```cpp
// check if a point lies within a convex triangle
template <typename N>
bool Earcut<N>::pointInTriangle(double ax, double ay, double bx, double by,
                                double cx, double cy, double px, double py) const {
    return (cx - px) * (ay - py) - (ax - px) * (cy - py) >= 0 &&
           (ax - px) * (by - py) - (bx - px) * (ay - py) >= 0 &&
           (bx - px) * (cy - py) - (cx - px) * (by - py) >= 0;
}
```

Three cross products, in the cyclic order **(c,a) → (a,b) → (b,c)**, each `>= 0` (boundary-inclusive), short-circuit `&&`. The operand order inside each term is exactly `(X - px) * (Y - py) - (Z - px) * (W - py)`; do **not** reorder — with doubles this is exact-sign only when no cancellation, and the fractal input does hit near-degenerate triangles.

